## In production

With `APP_ENV=production` the app refuses to start with unsafe settings (short secrets,
`CORS_ORIGINS=["*"]`{{ ", SQLite or no `DATABASE_URL`" if options.db else "" }}), turns off `/docs`, `/redoc` and
`/openapi.json` unless `DOCS_ENABLED=true`, and answers 501 for every operation whose
handler still returns example data. Every response carries security headers; request
bodies over `MAX_BODY_BYTES` get 413; validation errors say where and why without echoing
the input; unexpected errors answer a bare JSON 500{{ ", and database conflicts a 409" if options.db else "" }}.
{% if has_bearer %}

Bearer, OAuth2 and OpenID Connect tokens are JSON Web Tokens verified with `JWT_SECRET`
(HS256, HS384 or HS512), not with keys fetched from the provider (JWKS); replace
`_verify_jwt` in `app/auth.py` to use your identity provider's keys.
{% endif %}

## Configuration

| Variable | |
| --- | --- |
| `APP_ENV` | `development`, `test` or `production` (production refuses unsafe settings) |
| `CORS_ORIGINS` | JSON list of browser origins allowed to call the API |
| `DOCS_ENABLED` | Serve `/docs`, `/redoc` and `/openapi.json` (default: on, off in production) |
| `MAX_BODY_BYTES` | Largest request body in bytes, 413 above it (10 MiB; 0 turns it off) |
{% if has_bearer %}
| `JWT_SECRET` | Secret that signs and verifies bearer tokens (at least 32 characters in production) |
| `JWT_ALGORITHM`, `JWT_AUDIENCE`, `JWT_ISSUER` | Token algorithm (HS256, HS384 or HS512), optional audience and issuer |
| `JWT_LEEWAY_SECONDS` | Clock skew allowed on `exp` and `nbf` (30) |
{% endif %}
{% if has_apikey %}
| `API_KEYS` | JSON list of accepted API keys |
{% endif %}
{% if has_basic %}
| `BASIC_USERS` | JSON object of basic auth users and passwords |
{% endif %}
{% if options.db %}
| `DATABASE_URL` | SQLAlchemy URL (SQLite by default, Postgres in Docker Compose; required in production) |
| `DB_POOL_SIZE`, `DB_MAX_OVERFLOW`, `DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS` | Postgres connection pool (5, 10) and query timeout (30000 ms) |
{% endif %}

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` for local development.
